# Exhaustive Implementation Plan — Naga Bakes Offline Billing App

This plan provides a 100% complete, feature-by-feature specification for building **Naga Bakes**, a fully offline, icon/photo-first billing application designed for a non-literate, non-tech-savvy bakery/tea shop owner.

---

## 1. Requirement & Feature Matrix

| Feature Category | Master Prompt Requirement | Implementation Strategy |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **User Experience** | Icon & photo-first UI, large touch targets (≥64dp), zero typing except product name | Custom touch keypad, image picker, +/- steppers, high contrast colors |
| **Offline & Reliability** | Zero internet, zero login, zero backend, silent crash auto-recovery | Hive local database + path_provider file storage with try-catch auto-recovery wrappers |
| **State & Router** | Riverpod (`riverpod_annotation`, `riverpod_generator`), AutoRoute (`auto_route_generator`) | Clean Architecture state providers & generated type-safe routes |
| **Design System** | Strict zero-hardcoding policy (`AppColors`, `AppSpacing`, `AppTextStyles`, `AppSizes`, `AppRadius`, `AppShadows`, `AppStrings`, `AppAssets`) | Centralized design system with Runtime Light & Dark mode support |
| **Responsive Grid** | Scalable layout across phones (360x800) and tablets (800x1280, 1280x800) | `Breakpoints` + `ResponsiveBuilder` (2 columns phone, 4 columns tablet) |
| **PDF & Sharing** | Offline PDF invoice generation, printing & sharing | `pdf`, `printing`, `share_plus` packages |
| **Testing** | Pure Dart domain unit tests + reusable widget tests | `flutter_test`, `mocktail` |

